{"backgroundInformation":"The Lemon Model describes the underlying dynamics of a used car market where over time defective used cars (lemons) represent the bulk inventory of a used car lot. A 1970 paper entitled \"The Market for Lemons: Quality Uncertainty and the Market Mechanism\" describes this scenario as an example of how information asymmetry creates barriers to efficient markets. The Market for Lemons starts with a used car market containing both good quality and defective used cars. But because of asymmetric information about the car (the seller knows much more about the problems of the car than the buyer), the buyer of a car does not know beforehand whether it is a good car or a lemon. So the buyer's best guess for a given car is that the car is of average quality; accordingly, the buyer is only willing to pay the average value of a good car and a lemon. For example, if a good car is valued at $15000 and a lemon is valued at $10,000, ceteris paribus, the buyer of the used car will only pay $13,500 dollars for the used car. This difference in price creates a disincentive for car owners that possess good cars to sell their car to a dealer because the dealer is not willing to pay a high enough price to make the deal worth while. As a result, the average quality of the used car lot inventory decreases with time as do respective sales.","@type":"XMILEModel","modelId":"Lemon_model","sourceFile":"Lemon_model.xmile","simSpecs":{"method":"RK4","time_units":"Year","start":"0","stop":"365","dt":"1"},"variables":[{"type":"stock","name":"Total_Car_Quality","units":"Quality","eqn":"Normal_Quality*Initial_Cars_in_Lot","inflows":["Increase in Car Quality"],"outflows":["Decrease in Car Quality"]},{"type":"stock","name":"Used_Cars_in_Lot","units":"Cars","eqn":"Initial_Cars_in_Lot","inflows":["Cars Sold to Lot"],"outflows":["Car Bought from Lot"]},{"type":"aux","name":"Average_Car_Quality","units":"Quality/Car","eqn":"Total_Car_Quality/Used_Cars_in_Lot"},{"type":"aux","name":"Buy_Price","units":"Dollars/Car","eqn":"GAME ( Normal_Buy_Price)"},{"type":"aux","name":"Car_Bought_from_Lot","units":"Cars/Year","eqn":"Cars_Sold"},{"type":"aux","name":"Cars_Sold","units":"Cars/Year","eqn":"Normal_Cars_Sold*(Average_Car_Quality/Normal_Quality)*(Normal_Sell_Price/Sell_Price)"},{"type":"aux","name":"Cars_Sold_to_Lot","units":"Cars/Year","eqn":"0.8*50"},{"type":"aux","name":"Decrease_in_Car_Quality","units":"Quality/Year","eqn":"Average_Car_Quality*Car_Bought_from_Lot"},{"type":"aux","name":"Increase_in_Car_Quality","units":"Quality/Year","eqn":"Cars_Sold_to_Lot*Quality_Per_Car_Sold"},{"type":"aux","name":"Normal_Cars_Sold","units":"Cars/Year","eqn":"0.8*50"},{"type":"aux","name":"Normal_Sell_Price","units":"Dollars/Car","eqn":"Normal_Buy_Price*1.2"},{"type":"aux","name":"Quality_Per_Car_Sold","units":"Quality/Car","eqn":"Normal_Quality*(Buy_Price/Normal_Buy_Price)"},{"type":"aux","name":"Sell_Price","units":"Dollars/Car","eqn":"GAME ( Normal_Sell_Price)"},{"type":"aux","name":"Initial_Cars_in_Lot","units":"Cars","eqn":"2000"},{"type":"aux","name":"Normal_Buy_Price","units":"Dollars/Car","eqn":"15000"},{"type":"aux","name":"Normal_Quality","units":"Quality/Car","eqn":"1"}]}